From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 15:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scope tick-staging buffers per dispatch so parallel worlds
 compose

Replace the process-global ACTIVE buffer set in RegionTickStaging with a
per-dispatch Session that owns its own buffer collection. Each parallel
chunk-tick / entity-tick dispatch site creates a Session, threads it into
the region-worker closures (begin(session)), and drains ONLY that session in
applyAndClear(session, world). Two worlds ticking concurrently can no longer
have one world's serial replay touch the other world's staged writes.

In applyAndClear, route each replayed setBlock through the region that owns
the target chunk: inline fast path when the calling (owning) thread already
leases it (the common case, since the full-level lease is restored before
replay), otherwise hand the write to the owning region's mailbox via
OwnerDomainExecutor so it lands on the lease-holder instead of tripping the
AsyncCatcher owner-domain guard. Deferred-event ordering and the
veto-before-write cancellation gate are unchanged.

Serial/default path (parallel flags off) is byte-identical; no new -D flag.


